  "decision_conditions": [
    "The application as submitted comprises of inconsistent plans\r\nand insufficient detailing, relating to (i) a location plan which fails to\r\ndemonstrate all land necessary to carry out the proposed development, (ii) an inconsistent\r\nrear elevation which fails to illustrate the balustrade at first floor level\r\nand areas of urban greening at first and second floor.&nbsp; As such it is not\r\npossible to establish that the development complies with Policy 53 and 57 of\r\nthe Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).\r\n",
    "The proposed development provides a sub-standard level of accommodation for future occupiers, comprising of (i) combined kitchen, dining and living facility that fails to comply with minimum space standards (ii) Gross internal floor space which fails to provide adequate space for a 1 bedroom 2 person dwelling (iii) a proposal failing to provide an appropriate amount of well designed, suitably located and usable private or communal amenity space. Therefore, the proposal would be contrary to Policy 56 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024), Policy D6 of The London Plan (2021) and London Plan Guidance – Housing Design Standards (June 2023).",
    "Due to the setback nature of the application site from the public highway when accessed from the rear between 3 Bromley Road and 608 Lea Bridge Road the proposal fails to demonstrate a safe or welcoming environment for residents. Therefore, the proposal in its current form could be detrimental to pedestrian safety, as well as the well-being of future occupiers, contrary to Policy 58 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "The proposed development lacks architectural merit and is considered to result in a poor quality design which fails to enhance the local character and contribute positively to the streetscene and wider conservation area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy 53 and 72 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "The application as submitted comprises an over concentration of self contained studio dwellings without adequate justification, failing to respond to the identified housing need of the borough,&nbsp;contrary to Policy 15 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "The proposed development fails to incorporate an accessible step-free secure cycle storage contrary to Policy 61 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024) and London Cycling Design Standards (2014).",
    "The proposed development fails to provide accessible and adaptable dwellings in line with Building Regulation M4(2) contrary to Policy 16 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "In the absence of an adequate Daylight and Sunlight Assessment, to identify the impact of the development on the existing surrounding residential buildings a full assessment of the acceptability of the development could not be carried out, and therefore it cannot be confirmed that the development would be in compliance with ﻿Policy 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "In the absence of an adequate Daylight and Sunlight Assessment, to identify whether the proposed dwellings would receive adequate natural light to all habitable rooms, it cannot be confirmed that the development would be in compliance with ﻿Policy 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "In the absence of a satisfactory Outline Construction Logistic Plan, a full assessment of how the proposed development would be built or serviced without severely affecting the public highway could not be made in line with Policies T7 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy 65 of the emerging Local Plan.",
    "The applicant failed to enter into a s106 agreement and therefore not in compliance with Policy 94 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024)&nbsp;and the Waltham Forest Supplementary Planning Document “Planning Obligations” SPD, specifically in relation to the following planning obligations requirements (figures applicable at the time of the assessment of the application):car free developmenta contribution of £4,000 towards improving sustainable modes of transport£250 contribution towards the monitoring of the CLP£2,508.00&nbsp;towards Strategic Access Management and Monitoring measures (SAMMs)&nbsp;Highway condition surveySection 278 works"
  ],
